  "content": {
    "id": "p22-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "Let $f(x)=2^x+3$ and $g(x)=-3^x-2$. Find the range of",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p22-q8a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$f\\circ g$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(3,\\tfrac{13}{4})$.\n\nUse $g(x)<-2$ in the increasing function $f$.",
          "worked": "Since $3^x>0$, $g(x)$ takes every value in $(-\\infty,-2)$. Hence\n$$\\begin{align*}(f\\circ g)(x)&=2^{g(x)}+3,\\\\0&<2^{g(x)}<\\tfrac14,\\\\3&<(f\\circ g)(x)<\\tfrac{13}{4}.\\end{align*}$$\nBoth endpoints are excluded. The range is $(3,\\tfrac{13}{4})$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q8b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$g\\circ f$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(-\\infty,-29)$.\n\nUse $f(x)>3$ in the decreasing function $g$.",
          "worked": "The range of $f$ is $(3,\\infty)$. Therefore\n$$\\begin{align*}(g\\circ f)(x)&=-3^{f(x)}-2,\\\\3^{f(x)}&>27,\\\\(g\\circ f)(x)&<-29.\\end{align*}$$\nThe values approach $-29$ without reaching it and are unbounded below. The range is $(-\\infty,-29)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      }
    ]
  },
